<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3398" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		arca, I. B., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to a
			money-box</i> or <i>ready money</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gai.
					Inst. 1</span></i>
			. 3, § 131 Goes.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcārĭus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a treasurer</i>
			(late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcarii gazae tuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Esth. 3, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcarius civitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					Rom. 16, 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 40, 5, 41</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Also,</span>”
				<i>a controller of public revenues</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex. Sev. 43</span></i>
			.</div>
